<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sodasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sodasa was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-scythians">Indo-Scythian</a> ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mathura">Mathura</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, son of the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajuvula">Rajuvula</a>, in the early 1st century CE. Inscriptions in Brahmi from his reign record donations including a temple and gateway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasudeva">Vasudeva</a>, among the earliest records of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishnavism">Vaishnavism</a>, as well as Jain and Buddhist gifts. He also issued coins.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sodasa.jpg" alt="Sodasa" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Smith, Vincent A. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sodasa_coin_from_Mathura.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
